557 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 216 0 R
/T (Visakh Refinery, l ocated on the east coast of India at Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh, is the oldest refinery on the eastern seaboard and the first major industrial establishment in the city. It was originally commissioned in 1957 as Caltex Oil Refining \(India\) Limited \(CORIL\) with an installed capacity of 0.675 MMTPA. Following nationalization of Caltex's Indian operations in 1976, the refinery was amalgamated with HPCL in 1978.)
/E (Visakh Refinery, l ocated on the east coast of India at Visakhapatnam, Andhra Pradesh, is the oldest refinery on the eastern seaboard and the first major industrial establishment in the city. It was originally commissioned in 1957 as Caltex Oil Refining \(India\) Limited \(CORIL\) with an installed capacity of 0.675 MMTPA. Following nationalization of Caltex's Indian operations in 1976, the refinery was amalgamated with HPCL in 1978.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
558 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 216 0 R
/T (The refinery has undergone successive phases of capacity expansion and technological upgradation: 1.5 MMTPA through debottlenecking in the years following nationalization, 4.5 MMTPA in 1985 with the commissioning of a second crude train and an FCC Unit, 7.5 MMTPA in 1999 under the Visakh Refinery Expansion Project \(VREP-II\) together with a Diesel Hydro-Desulphurization \(DHDS\) unit, and 8.3 MMTPA by 2010 with the addition of Diesel Hydrotreating \(DHT\) facilities and the associated MS-quality upgradation block.)
/E (The refinery has undergone successive phases of capacity expansion and technological upgradation: 1.5 MMTPA through debottlenecking in the years following nationalization, 4.5 MMTPA in 1985 with the commissioning of a second crude train and an FCC Unit, 7.5 MMTPA in 1999 under the Visakh Refinery Expansion Project \(VREP-II\) together with a Diesel Hydro-Desulphurization \(DHDS\) unit, and 8.3 MMTPA by 2010 with the addition of Diesel Hydrotreating \(DHT\) facilities and the associated MS-quality upgradation block.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
559 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 216 0 R
/T (Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited \(HPCL\) is a Maharatna Central Public Sector Enterprise under the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas, Government of India, and is the second-largest integrated oil refining and marketing company in the country. HPCL's business segments span crude oil refining, marketing of petroleum products \(retail, industrial, aviation and lubricants\), LPG distribution, cross-country pipeline transportation, and an expanding portfolio of petrochemicals, city gas distribution and renewable energy. HPCL holds close to 20% of India's refining market share and operates an extensive marketing infrastructure comprising retail outlets, LPG bottling plants, aviation fuel stations, lube blending plants and cross-country pipelines.)
/E (Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited \(HPCL\) is a Maharatna Central Public Sector Enterprise under the Ministry of Petroleum and Natural Gas, Government of India, and is the second-largest integrated oil refining and marketing company in the country. HPCL's business segments span crude oil refining, marketing of petroleum products \(retail, industrial, aviation and lubricants\), LPG distribution, cross-country pipeline transportation, and an expanding portfolio of petrochemicals, city gas distribution and renewable energy. HPCL holds close to 20% of India's refining market share and operates an extensive marketing infrastructure comprising retail outlets, LPG bottling plants, aviation fuel stations, lube blending plants and cross-country pipelines.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
