/T (Saturates: paraffinic and naphthenic hydrocarbons, low polarity, good hydrogen-donor character during hydroprocessing. Aromatics: mono- and polynuclear aromatic ring systems; a significant proportion is converted to lighter products but also contributes to coke precursors at high aromaticity. Resins: polar, moderately high molecular weight molecules containing heteroatoms \(S, N, O\) that act as peptizing \(stabilizing\) agents for asphaltenes in the oil matrix. Asphaltenes: the highest molecular weight, most polar, most condensed polynuclear-aromatic fraction, insoluble in n-heptane/n-pentane; the principal precursor of coke and catalyst-fouling deposits during)
/E (Saturates: paraffinic and naphthenic hydrocarbons, low polarity, good hydrogen-donor character during hydroprocessing. Aromatics: mono- and polynuclear aromatic ring systems; a significant proportion is converted to lighter products but also contributes to coke precursors at high aromaticity. Resins: polar, moderately high molecular weight molecules containing heteroatoms \(S, N, O\) that act as peptizing \(stabilizing\) agents for asphaltenes in the oil matrix. Asphaltenes: the highest molecular weight, most polar, most condensed polynuclear-aromatic fraction, insoluble in n-heptane/n-pentane; the principal precursor of coke and catalyst-fouling deposits during)
/Pg 27 0 R
