<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 222 0 R
/E (Nickel and vanadium, present in residue predominantly as metalloporphyrin complexes, are of particular concern because they deposit irreversibly on catalyst surfaces during hydroprocessing and catalytic cracking, blocking active sites and pore mouths \(metal poisoning\) and, in the case of vanadium, promoting dehydrogenation side reactions that increase hydrogen and coke yields. Metals content is therefore a primary basis for selecting between disposable- catalyst thermal routes, catalyst-replenishing ebullated-bed hydrocracking, and metal-rejecting solvent deasphalting)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [4]
>>
