/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 225 0 R
/T (Two configurations are used industrially: coil \(furnace\) visbreaking, in which cracking occurs in the radiant coil of a fired heater followed by rapid quench, and soaker visbreaking, in which the feed is heated to a lower coil-outlet temperature and then held in an insulated soaker drum for extended residence time, achieving comparable conversion at lower temperature and hence lower energy consumption and fuel-gas make.)
/E (Two configurations are used industrially: coil \(furnace\) visbreaking, in which cracking occurs in the radiant coil of a fired heater followed by rapid quench, and soaker visbreaking, in which the feed is heated to a lower coil-outlet temperature and then held in an insulated soaker drum for extended residence time, achieving comparable conversion at lower temperature and hence lower energy consumption and fuel-gas make.)
/Pg 31 0 R
/K [29]
>>
