/T (Because residue feeds carry substantially more CCR-forming material and metal contaminants \(Ni, V\) than VGO, RFCC units require significant hardware and catalyst modifications relative to standard FCC: a two-stage or high- efficiency regenerator to manage the higher coke burn and heat release; feed nozzles designed for improved atomization of the heavier feed; a catalyst cooler to remove excess regenerator heat; higher catalyst circulation and makeup rates to counteract metal poisoning and maintain activity; and metals-passivation additives \(e.g., antimony- or bismuth based\) mitigate the dehydrogenation activity of deposited of vanadium.)
/E (Because residue feeds carry substantially more CCR-forming material and metal contaminants \(Ni, V\) than VGO, RFCC units require significant hardware and catalyst modifications relative to standard FCC: a two-stage or high- efficiency regenerator to manage the higher coke burn and heat release; feed nozzles designed for improved atomization of the heavier feed; a catalyst cooler to remove excess regenerator heat; higher catalyst circulation and makeup rates to counteract metal poisoning and maintain activity; and metals-passivation additives \(e.g., antimony- or bismuth based\) mitigate the dehydrogenation activity of deposited of vanadium.)
/Pg 35 0 R
/K [2]
