/T (Advantages: Low operating temperature \(thermally mild, essentially no cracking or coke formation\); effective concentration/rejection of metals, CCR and asphaltenes into a small pitch stream, upgrading the bulk of the residue \(as DAO\) to a quality acceptable as feed to RFCC, hydrocracking, or lube-base-oil manufacture; relatively low capital  cost compared to hydrogen-addition routes.)
/E (Advantages: Low operating temperature \(thermally mild, essentially no cracking or coke formation\); effective concentration/rejection of metals, CCR and asphaltenes into a small pitch stream, upgrading the bulk of the residue \(as DAO\) to a quality acceptable as feed to RFCC, hydrocracking, or lube-base-oil manufacture; relatively low capital  cost compared to hydrogen-addition routes.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
