1509 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 248 0 R
/E (Residue upgradation has evolved from a peripheral refinery activity concerned chiefly with viscosity and pour- point reduction of fuel oil, into one of the central strategic and technological pillars of modern petroleum refining. The structural decline of high-sulphur fuel-oil demand, the tightening of clean-fuel regulation \(culminating, in the Indian context, in BS-VI norms\), and the direct economic incentive to extract maximum distillate value from every barrel of crude have together made deep bottom-of-the-barrel conversion an operational necessity for globally competitive refiners.)
/Pg 54 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
