/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 249 0 R
/E (Beyond its immediate technical and economic significance, the RUF project illustrates the broader trajectory of the Indian refining sector: increasing refinery complexity and crude-flexibility, deepening integration of hydroprocessing across the barrel, growing reliance on digital process optimization, and a gradual but decisive shift away from residual fuel oil towards a distillate- and petrochemical-oriented product slate. As the industry looks towards an eventual low-carbon future, the hydrogen infrastructure, deep-conversion capability and digital optimization platforms established through projects such as HPCL's RUF are likely to serve as a foundation for the next generation of sustainable, integrated refining-petrochemical-hydrogen complexes in India.)
/Pg 55 0 R
/K [16]
>>
