/Title (This report presents a comprehensive technical study of residue upgradation technologies employed in modern petroleum refineries, undertaken during an industrial internship at Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Limited \(HPCL\), Visakh Refinery. The report begins with an overview of HPCL and the historical evolution of the Visakh Refinery, including the Visakh Refinery Modernization Project \(VRMP\), which enhanced the refinery's crude processing capacity to 15 MMTPA and its Nelson Complexity Index to 11.6.)
